{
  "result": "On Tuesday the laundromat acquired a piano. It stood between the change machine and a dryer that had been out of order since Christmas. Nobody knew who had brought it. By noon someone had set a bottle of detergent on top, which made it seem as though it had belonged.\n\nThe first person to play was a boy waiting for his father to fold towels. He pressed the lowest key and looked over his shoulder, delighted to have made a noise no one could reasonably blame on him. His father kept folding. The boy tried the highest key. Same result.\n\nLater a woman in hospital scrubs sat down and played the first eight bars of a song I knew but couldn\u2019t name. She stopped at the same place three times. On the fourth try, a man sorting socks hummed what came next. She turned around. \u201cIs that it?\u201d she asked.\n\nHe said he didn\u2019t know either. His mother used to sing something like it while she cooked. He hummed the bit, and the woman found two notes that fit. Then her dryer buzzed. She got up, and he held the door while she carried her basket out to the car.\n\nA week later the piano was gone. The owner told me it had been delivered to the wrong address. I asked where it was supposed to go, and he pointed toward the music school. Through the window I could see a handwritten sign propped on the lid: *Please do not touch.*",
